# safety-guard.conf — destructive-action gate config.
# Installed to ~/.config/safety-guard.conf; read by scripts/lib/safety-guard.sh.
# Parsed as KEY=VALUE, NEVER sourced, and NEVER read from the caller's environment
# (an agent must not be able to widen its own limits in the same call it makes).
# Holds no secrets.
#
# SAFETY_ALLOWLIST: space-separated command words the OWNER has chosen to exempt
# from the destructive-action gate. EMPTY IS THE SUPPORTED DEFAULT — every command
# the classifier flags is confirmed by a human. Exempt a verb only per-verb, after
# weighing BOTH blast radius and cost (see docs/PROJECT.md), never as a shortcut.
SAFETY_ALLOWLIST=
